{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And to his son.</b> Meaning — he did not designate her for himself, but his son desires her. Scripture informs us that he may designate her, and it says <b>he shall designate her</b>, meaning, the money of her purchase shall serve as her designation, whether to himself or to his son, and no money for kiddushin is required." "And its saying <b>according to the law of daughters</b>, meaning, whether he designated her for himself or for his son, he must fulfill the law of daughters, which is what it states nearby: ״שְׁאֵרָהּ״ etc."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:31:36.530303801Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}